==Esperanto==

===Etymology===
{{m|eo|ki-||interrogative and relative [[:Category:Esperanto correlatives|correlative]] prefix}} + {{m|eo|-u||correlative suffix of individuals}}

===Pronunciation===
{{eo-IPA|a=Eo-kiu.ogg}}

===Pronoun===
{{head|eo|pronoun|cat2=correlatives|plural|kiuj|accusative singular|kiun|accusative plural|kiujn}}

# [[who]] (the interrogative and relative correlative of individuals)
#* {{quote-journal|eo|date=29 Dec 73|volume=1|number=28|journal=Gay Community News|page=10|author=J. C. Kilburn|title=Esperantistoj! (personal advertisement)|text=Iu, '''kiu''' dezirus korespondi kun eksterlandaj gesamseksemuloj, bonvole skribu al {{...}}}}
#: {{ux|eo|Mi jam diris, ke mia frato, '''kiu''' estis iomete pli aĝa ol mi, mortis.|I already said, that my brother, '''who''' was a little bit older than me, died.}}
# {{lb|eo|relative}} [[which]]
#: {{ux|eo|La vivo moviĝas laŭ bova rapideco sur la sunaj, ĉielgloraj deklivoj, '''kiuj''' falas de la piramidaj pintoj al la bordoj de la bluega oceano.
|t=Life moves ploddingly on the sunny, heavenly-glorious slopes, '''which''' fall from the piramidal peaks to the borders of the big blue ocean.}}
#: ''Karlo restas fama pro la influo-batalo, '''kiun''' li entreprenis kontraŭ la Parlamento de Anglio.''<sup>({{w|lang=eo|Karlo la 1-a (Anglio)|VP}})</sup>
#:: Charles remains famous for the influence battle, '''which''' he undertook against the English Parliament.

====Derived terms====
* {{l|eo|kiu ajn|gloss=[[whoever]]}}

===Determiner===
{{eo-det}}

# [[which]], [[what]]

===Usage notes===
Like other interrogative and relative correlatives, '''kiu''' can be combined with {{m|eo|ajn}}, the adverbial particle of generality. '''Kiu ajn''' thus means ''[[whoever]]''.

